  "version": "0.1.4",
  "notes": "### Added\n- Notes can belong to a project, and each project page lists its notes.\n- Money: hide amounts with the eye button; showing them again asks for your Vault master password.\n- Money: edit or delete savings and investment accounts, and delete goals.\n- Ask Pyxida can search the web when your workspace doesn't have the answer, and shows its sources. You can turn this off in Settings.\n- Notes: Vim yank and paste use the system clipboard, and a new Wrap lines setting (off on computers by default).\n- Phone reminders show the task title and time.\n\n### Changed\n- The phone and web app save only what changed, so typing stays fast in large workspaces, and unsaved text survives the app being closed in the background.\n- Sync is much faster with thousands of files and no longer freezes the window.\n- Delete a project directly from its page.\n\n### Fixed\n- The phone app no longer shows a blank screen after an update.\n- Weather works for home locations written with a country, such as \"Γιαννιτσά, Ελλάδα\".\n- Adding an event to Google Calendar without a connection now shows an error instead of claiming success; new events default to Google only when it is connected.\n- Long task descriptions no longer overflow the task dialog.\n- Money keeps extra columns in your CSV files, and one damaged line no longer hides a whole year.\n- Editing a project keeps any extra details in its file.\n- If a task changed elsewhere while its dialog was open, you get a warning instead of overwriting it.\n- Events that run past midnight also show on the next day.\n- Notes save before the window closes, and a note moved to the trash can no longer come back.",
